icit GPU resource and command-queue management - device/context creation, buffer allocation, kernel launch/dispatch. Kept separate from graphics_rendering (OpenGL's immediate-mode-ish draw calls): CUDA/OpenCL/Vulkan all share the same \"manage device, buffer, queue, command, then submit\" shape even though Vulkan also renders. Intel oneAPI/SYCL is intentionally NOT padded with guessed names here - it's a header-only C++ template API (sycl::queue, sycl::buffer, parallel_for as methods/lambdas), not free functions, so it isn't reliably caught by this project's call-name matching; that gap is honest, not an oversight.\n",languages:{c:["cudaMalloc","cudaFree","cudaMemcpy","cudaMemcpyAsync","cudaDeviceSynchronize","cudaLaunchKernel","cudaStreamCreate","cudaStreamDestroy","cudaEventCreate","cudaEventRecord","cudaGetLastError","cudaGetDeviceCount","clGetPlatformIDs","clGetDeviceIDs","clCreateContext","clCreateCommandQueue","clCreateBuffer","clCreateProgramWithSource","clBuildProgram","clCreateKernel","clSetKernelArg","clEnqueueNDRangeKernel","clEnqueueReadBuffer","clEnqueueWriteBuffer","clFinish","clReleaseContext","clReleaseCommandQueue","vkCreateInstance","vkDestroyInstance","vkCreateDevice","vkDestroyDevice","vkCreateBuffer","vkAllocateMemory","vkCreateCommandPool","vkAllocateCommandBuffers","vkBeginCommandBuffer","vkEndCommandBuffer","vkCmdDraw","vkCmdDispatch","vkQueueSubmit","vkCreateSwapchainKHR","vkCreateShaderModule","vkCreateGraphicsPipelines","cudaMallocHost","cudaMallocManaged","cudaMallocPitch","cudaFreeHost","cudaMemcpy2D","cudaMemcpyToSymbol","cudaMemcpyFromSymbol","cudaMemset","cudaMemsetAsync","cudaMemGetInfo","cudaStreamCreateWithFlags","cudaStreamSynchronize","cudaStreamWaitEvent","cudaEventSynchronize","cudaEventElapsedTime","cudaEventDestroy","cudaGetDeviceProperties","cudaSetDevice","cudaGetDevice","cudaGetErrorString","cudaPeekAtLastError","cudaLaunchCooperativeKernel","cudaGraphCreate","cudaGraphLaunch","cudaStreamBeginCapture","cudaStreamEndCapture