ve document model, not a widget toolkit, and separate from event_handling (listening for/reacting to events is a different concern from shaping the tree itself). Honest trade-off: several entries here (`appendChild`, `remove`, `closest`, `matches`) are bare DOM method names with no receiver qualification - a class that happens to define its OWN method of the same name (e.g. a custom `remove()`) would be misclassified the same way any bare-name category entry can be, in any language; not attempting per-receiver-type resolution (not statically knowable without a type system) is a documented scope limit, not an oversight.",languages:{c:[],java:[],python:[],javascript:["document.getElementById","document.querySelector","document.querySelectorAll","document.createElement","document.createTextNode","querySelector","querySelectorAll","appendChild","removeChild","insertBefore","replaceChild","remove","closest","matches","setAttribute","getAttribute","removeAttribute","classList.add","classList.remove","classList.toggle","classList.contains","cloneNode","document.createDocumentFragment","document.createElementNS","document.getElementsByClassName","document.getElementsByTagName","document.getElementsByName","document.elementFromPoint","document.elementsFromPoint","document.write","document.writeln","document.open","document.close","document.execCommand","document.adoptNode","document.importNode","hasAttribute","toggleAttribute","classList.replace","replaceWith","append","prepend","before","after","insertAdjacentHTML","insertAdjacentElement","insertAdjacentText","getBoundingClientRect","scrollIntoView","focus","blur","click","style.setProperty","getComputedStyle","innerHTML"],html:[]}},event_handling:{label:"Event listener registration / dispatch",description:'Registers, removes, or manually fires a DOM/browser event, or intercepts its default behavior/propagation - a distinct concern from dom_manipulation (shaping the tree) and from asynchronous control flow (concurrency cate